\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {35}{\ignorespaces Stochastic volatility, parameter learning: observation-scale fitting and likelihood score. $N{=}128$; $y_t=s\exp (x_t/2)\eta _t$ with true scale $s^\star {=}1$; 50 steps, resampling when ESS $<0.5N$. $\hat  s$ maximizes the PF log-likelihood over the grid $\{0.6,0.8,1.0,1.2,1.4\}$ with common random numbers; $\hat  s_{\mathrm  {grid}}$ is the maximizer for a 1001-point numerical grid filter. The score is a central difference in $\log s$ ($\delta {=}0.01$) at $s{=}1$, compared with the grid-filter score. Mean $\pm $ 95\% CI over 10 observation sequences.}}{48}{}\protected@file@percent }
